---
title: Vanilla Cream Pudding (with Variants)
servings: 4
image: https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Vanilla-Pudding-V1.jpg
---

Blend @sugar{1/3%cup}, @cornstarch{2%tbsp}, and @salt{1/8%tsp} in #2-quart sauce pan{}.

Combine @milk{2%cups} and @egg yolks{2}(slightly beaten), and gradually stir into sugar mixture.

Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until mixture thickens and boils.

Boil and stir for ~{1%minute}.

Remove from heat; stir in @butter{2%tbsp}(softened) and @vanilla{2%tsp}.

Pour into dessert dishes. Cover.

Cool slightly before serving.

== Butterscotch Variant ==

Substitute 2/3 cup brown sugar (packed) for the granulated sugar.

== Chocolate Variant ==

Increase the sugar to 1/2 cup and stir 1/3 cup cocoa into the sugar-cornstarch mixture. Omit the butter.